WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.083 --> 00:00:01.626
I am so freaking excited.

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:03.169
I think this is the best content
we've ever filmed.

00:00:03.253 --> 00:00:05.422
By the end of today,
someone's gonna win this $5,000,000.

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:07.799
A show this massive,
let's finish this out strong.

00:00:07.882 --> 00:00:08.717
We got a hell of a season.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.260
All our camera crew, turn around.

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:11.803
We're clearing everybody.
They got blindfolds.

00:00:11.886 --> 00:00:13.930
What about this BTS crew?
They got cameras everywhere.

00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:16.558
Our BTS crew is one of the few
who knows who won.

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:18.101
-All right, here we go.
-Heads up.

00:00:19.561 --> 00:00:22.564
You will be taking turns kicking balls
at each other's hearts.

00:00:22.647 --> 00:00:24.691
Kick for Hannah.
We're all kicking for Hannah.

00:00:24.774 --> 00:00:28.028
It is a sucky feeling,
the entire cast gang up against you.

00:00:28.111 --> 00:00:30.613
If your heart is smashed,
you will be eliminated.

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:31.865
This could be the kill shot.

00:00:38.121 --> 00:00:39.581
Look how big the studio is.

00:00:39.664 --> 00:00:41.082
We're all running on adrenaline.

00:00:41.166 --> 00:00:42.000
I'm tired as hell.

00:00:42.083 --> 00:00:43.668
I'm worried in the cut
I'm gonna look sleepy.

00:00:43.752 --> 00:00:44.669
Start the money counter!

00:00:44.753 --> 00:00:47.380
$600,000 and nobody's taking the bribes.

00:00:47.464 --> 00:00:48.923
They're nervous. It is what it is.

00:00:49.007 --> 00:00:50.008
That's a lot of money.

00:00:50.091 --> 00:00:51.509
My life is on the line.

00:00:51.593 --> 00:00:53.303
Things are feeling a bit tense.

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:54.596
A lot of these people
will leave with nothing.

00:00:54.679 --> 00:00:56.598
Do you get emotional at moments like this?

00:00:56.681 --> 00:00:59.017
Three, two, one...

00:00:59.768 --> 00:01:00.935
-Somebody pressed it?
-Yeah.

00:01:01.019 --> 00:01:02.145
Someone pressed it.

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:03.980
Sorry, bro. Nothing personal.

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:05.732
I owe you my life in this game.

00:01:07.192 --> 00:01:08.651
Two people, one shot.

00:01:09.527 --> 00:01:13.698
We officially have the winner
of Season 2 of &lt;i&gt;Beast Games!&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:16.993 --> 00:01:18.995
I am so freaking excited.

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:21.247
A, because I think this is
the best content we have ever filmed,

00:01:21.331 --> 00:01:24.084
and B, I just wanna sleep in a bed.

00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:25.168
Let's wrap it up.

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:26.628
Are you starting to sleep?

00:01:26.711 --> 00:01:27.545
No.

00:01:27.629 --> 00:01:29.297
My heart is beating too fast.

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:34.886
This is the actual $5,000,000 check.

00:01:34.969 --> 00:01:36.304
And I'm signing right here?

00:01:36.388 --> 00:01:37.263
All right.

00:01:37.347 --> 00:01:40.266
By the end of today,
someone's gonna win this $5,000,000.

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:41.893
This is what they win, not that cash.

00:01:41.976 --> 00:01:43.770
They would get robbed if I gave them cash.

00:01:43.853 --> 00:01:47.774
When we film,
it will be a cleared lockdown,

00:01:47.857 --> 00:01:49.526
no feeds on the outside.

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:51.361
There will be nobody hanging out here.

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:54.406
With a show this massive,
we really need to keep the integrity

00:01:54.489 --> 00:01:57.242
of who and what ends up happening
in this episode.

00:01:57.325 --> 00:01:58.993
So let's finish this out strong,

00:01:59.077 --> 00:02:00.495
'cause we got a hell of a season.

00:02:00.578 --> 00:02:03.206
Okay everybody,
we're closing doors between sets.

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:05.667
We're closing the doors between sets.

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:08.712
-Last day.
-Game day, baby.

00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:10.588
Lock in on your verbiage.
Can you please read that?

00:02:10.672 --> 00:02:11.965
We should go through it.

00:02:12.048 --> 00:02:14.050
This is the grand finale.
We want to build up what's happened,

00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:18.722
so these are detailed notes of everything
each contestant so far has done.

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:21.307
I'm just editing them
because this is a lot of word vomit.

00:02:21.391 --> 00:02:23.810
You think you have the individual talents
to bring it home?

00:02:23.893 --> 00:02:25.395
Yeah, see that's too much.

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:28.606
We have their entire story,
every single episode.

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:29.649
Yeah, very important.

00:02:29.733 --> 00:02:32.986
It's like, "You got through the Smart Game
at this time."

00:02:33.069 --> 00:02:35.905
And just build up your tone
as you get to the end.

00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:38.825
"All bringing you
to this moment right here."

00:02:38.908 --> 00:02:41.870
We're good to bring in the contestants
if everyone's quiet.

00:02:41.953 --> 00:02:43.705
-Does this give you guys PTSD?
-Yeah.

00:02:43.788 --> 00:02:45.248
Yes, it definitely does.

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:46.875
All right, Darius,
lock in when we're done.

00:02:46.958 --> 00:02:48.043
Let's do it.

00:02:48.126 --> 00:02:51.129
Things are getting set, we're about to get
started with Episode 10, the big finale.

00:02:51.212 --> 00:02:52.339
It's go time.

00:02:52.964 --> 00:02:56.009
So far in this season, after each game,
we started a timer.

00:02:56.092 --> 00:02:59.429
But for this game,
we're gonna jump right into it.

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:00.680
Open the door!

00:03:02.474 --> 00:03:04.309
Welcome to the grand finale

00:03:04.392 --> 00:03:10.190
where one of you is gonna be winning
that $5,000,000, right here, right now.

00:03:11.733 --> 00:03:14.986
You'll be taking turns kicking balls
at each other's hearts.

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:18.073
If your heart is smashed,
you will be eliminated.

00:03:18.615 --> 00:03:21.951
We're right below the set
of the first game of the finale.

00:03:22.035 --> 00:03:24.579
The hearts are over there,
the contestants are over there

00:03:24.662 --> 00:03:26.998
and things are feeling a bit tense

00:03:27.082 --> 00:03:29.334
because a lot of these people
will leave with nothing

00:03:29.417 --> 00:03:31.044
and one will leave with $5,000,000.

00:03:31.586 --> 00:03:32.545
All right, here we go.

00:03:33.171 --> 00:03:34.798
Tyler, when you are ready,

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:37.884
kick that ball at whatever heart you want.

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:43.014
I thought that hit it.

00:03:43.098 --> 00:03:45.975
Tyler's getting serious!
Look at that face.

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:47.477
He does not like that.

00:03:50.605 --> 00:03:52.482
Things are getting good.

00:04:01.449 --> 00:04:03.660
Everything just went silent

00:04:04.619 --> 00:04:06.371
and Jack is the first one
to be eliminated.

00:04:07.038 --> 00:04:08.581
Emotions are at an all-time high.

00:04:10.792 --> 00:04:12.502
That is literally
the worst feeling in the world.

00:04:13.795 --> 00:04:16.589
Jack, it was nothing personal, buddy.
I honestly mean that.

00:04:16.673 --> 00:04:17.882
You can say that all you want,

00:04:17.966 --> 00:04:19.676
but when the kick
goes right to your heart...

00:04:20.301 --> 00:04:21.636
Don't be crying when you say it.

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:23.013
-Drop him.
-Hit me.

00:04:25.432 --> 00:04:27.892
How about that? Five contestants remain,

00:04:27.976 --> 00:04:31.271
one of which will win
that $5,000,000 over there.

00:04:33.481 --> 00:04:36.651
Kind of went through the stages of grief
very quickly.

00:04:36.735 --> 00:04:38.611
When I look back on the show,

00:04:38.695 --> 00:04:40.905
hopefully I'm not gonna think about
that moment too much.

00:04:40.989 --> 00:04:43.700
But I'm gonna look back on
making it far enough

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:47.871
to give the opportunity to my mom
and my brother to come out here

00:04:47.954 --> 00:04:49.622
and share that moment with me.

00:04:49.706 --> 00:04:52.876
Having made it so far,
I hope they're proud of me.

00:04:55.712 --> 00:04:58.006
We still need to eliminate
one more of you.

00:04:58.089 --> 00:04:59.758
Brett, when you're ready.

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:04.179
It almost hit Cory!

00:05:07.057 --> 00:05:09.309
Kick for Hannah.
We're all kicking for Hannah.

00:05:10.518 --> 00:05:14.230
It is a sucky feeling, to have
the entire cast gang up against you.

00:05:15.106 --> 00:05:17.442
This could be it.
This could be the kill shot.

00:05:17.525 --> 00:05:18.568
Come on.

00:05:26.242 --> 00:05:31.331
We have the greatest episode of all time,
but are you out of your... What just...

00:05:31.414 --> 00:05:32.415
That was incredible.

00:05:32.499 --> 00:05:35.835
The first time he targets Auguste,
Auguste is out.

00:05:37.879 --> 00:05:39.297
I'm sorry, bro.

00:05:39.381 --> 00:05:43.468
Auguste, to me, like,
was the best student of the game.

00:05:43.551 --> 00:05:45.804
And I thought he would make it
to the final two.

00:05:45.887 --> 00:05:48.848
So to see him go out like this,
by one of his friends,

00:05:48.932 --> 00:05:51.309
seeing an alliance break
the last second like that

00:05:51.393 --> 00:05:52.894
is just devestating.

00:05:52.977 --> 00:05:54.771
I don't know why that had to happen
that way.

00:05:54.854 --> 00:05:57.649
We went through the whole game together.
That was the last thing I was expecting.

00:05:57.732 --> 00:05:58.566
I'm sorry.

00:06:00.235 --> 00:06:02.112
I don't know why you did that.

00:06:03.571 --> 00:06:04.906
I'm in shock.

00:06:07.158 --> 00:06:08.118
It's on your cue.

00:06:09.577 --> 00:06:10.578
Drop him.

00:06:12.914 --> 00:06:14.833
Never would have thought
that would happen.

00:06:14.916 --> 00:06:16.459
That's his alliance member.

00:06:16.543 --> 00:06:18.586
He just turned on him
and hit him, first try.

00:06:18.670 --> 00:06:19.879
I can't believe it.

00:06:19.963 --> 00:06:21.965
I cannot believe it.
I've never seen anything like it.

00:06:24.843 --> 00:06:26.845
-Sorry, bro.
-Appreciate you, bro.

00:06:27.345 --> 00:06:31.182
What's gonna affect you a lot
is walking away with nothing.

00:06:31.266 --> 00:06:35.103
The 41 days, the sacrifice,
the waste of time, all that.

00:06:35.186 --> 00:06:37.814
-Just know, man...
-This was 100% worth it.

00:06:37.897 --> 00:06:39.899
-I'm just like…
-There...

00:06:41.401 --> 00:06:44.696
Tyler, he's someone
who I've been close with.

00:06:44.779 --> 00:06:46.781
Pretty much every bus ride
we sat next to each other.

00:06:46.865 --> 00:06:48.992
He's the last person
I thought would go for me.

00:06:49.075 --> 00:06:51.786
And like that, when it's the closest
person to you on stage

00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:53.496
and so that just stinks.

00:06:54.372 --> 00:06:56.833
Auguste was a close friend of mine,
he still is.

00:06:56.916 --> 00:06:59.586
But he was a big threat too,
so it was a strategic play.

00:07:00.211 --> 00:07:03.506
What really got me to change my mind
was seeing Hannah in tears.

00:07:03.590 --> 00:07:05.050
A lot of us were going for her.

00:07:05.133 --> 00:07:08.636
I wouldn't want my boys at home
to gang up on someone.

00:07:09.220 --> 00:07:12.223
When it was everyone coming for me,
it just made me feel very alone.

00:07:12.307 --> 00:07:13.892
And it is a game, and I get it.

00:07:14.267 --> 00:07:16.478
But that was the hard part for me.

00:07:19.314 --> 00:07:21.691
How are we looking on cameras?
How long do we need?

00:07:23.902 --> 00:07:25.737
I say we proceed to the next game

00:07:25.820 --> 00:07:27.781
and eliminate another one of you.

00:07:29.616 --> 00:07:32.452
The drone is up.
They're about to play the second game.

00:07:32.535 --> 00:07:34.871
It's a combination of Strong and Smart.

00:07:34.954 --> 00:07:37.040
We'll see how long
they can hold onto the pole

00:07:37.123 --> 00:07:38.458
and if they can memorize the blocks.

00:07:38.541 --> 00:07:41.086
First person to touch their button

00:07:41.169 --> 00:07:44.047
will bring the platforms up
and have to come over here

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:47.842
and solve the 16-block pattern
from memory.

00:07:47.926 --> 00:07:50.720
If you rebuild it incorrectly,
you will be eliminated.

00:07:50.804 --> 00:07:51.971
Oh, my God.

00:07:53.890 --> 00:07:55.308
Drop their platforms!

00:07:55.392 --> 00:07:56.851
The game is on!

00:08:05.568 --> 00:08:07.487
You're good. You can step off.
Come over, Brett.

00:08:09.239 --> 00:08:10.949
So far, he's doing it from his own memory.

00:08:11.032 --> 00:08:12.367
No one's helped him.

00:08:12.450 --> 00:08:14.494
Hey, Russ, if it's right, turn it green,

00:08:14.577 --> 00:08:16.329
if it's wrong, turn it red. That's it.

00:08:17.372 --> 00:08:19.249
All right. It is officially locked in.

00:08:19.874 --> 00:08:20.959
He did it!

00:08:21.042 --> 00:08:24.754
Brett has now guaranteed a spot
in the top three.

00:08:25.088 --> 00:08:26.589
Now you three are on the chopping block.

00:08:26.673 --> 00:08:28.425
I can tell Brett is already stressed.

00:08:28.508 --> 00:08:31.344
But it's not official
until he smashes your heart.

00:08:31.428 --> 00:08:32.762
You have to drop it.

00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:34.597
In front of the person.

00:08:37.642 --> 00:08:39.310
Dude, really?

00:08:41.187 --> 00:08:44.024
I am so sorry, but Hannah,

00:08:44.107 --> 00:08:46.568
I am going to pick you.

00:08:47.068 --> 00:08:50.447
Obviously I'm heartbroken to be
about to be dropped to my death,

00:08:50.530 --> 00:08:53.700
but I feel okay leaving with
this combination of people.

00:08:53.783 --> 00:08:55.076
All right, whenever you're ready, Brett.

00:08:57.954 --> 00:08:59.205
All right, drop her.

00:09:01.166 --> 00:09:06.212
I'm honestly in shock. How did I make it
to the top four of &lt;i&gt;Beast Games &lt;/i&gt;Season 2?

00:09:06.296 --> 00:09:09.382
How was I the final female,
the final Smart person?

00:09:09.466 --> 00:09:11.760
That doesn't feel real.
When I applied, I was like,

00:09:11.843 --> 00:09:13.887
"Try not to be in the first 50% out."

00:09:13.970 --> 00:09:16.723
How did I get here? I don't understand.

00:09:17.891 --> 00:09:20.226
-For old times' sake.
-For old times' sake, get this...

00:09:22.270 --> 00:09:23.730
I didn't go limp, I'm sorry.

00:09:26.024 --> 00:09:27.067
You good?

00:09:27.817 --> 00:09:29.027
For old times' sake.

00:09:29.110 --> 00:09:30.153
All right, let's do it.

00:09:30.236 --> 00:09:32.655
We're about to eliminate one more of you.

00:09:32.739 --> 00:09:35.367
Welcome to the final bribe.

00:09:35.450 --> 00:09:37.243
We're working even later into the night,

00:09:37.327 --> 00:09:40.121
but we finally started our third game,
and that's the bribe.

00:09:40.205 --> 00:09:43.124
One of them could walk away
with $1,000,000 if they self-eliminate.

00:09:43.208 --> 00:09:44.334
Cuff them!

00:09:45.085 --> 00:09:46.670
I just handcuffed you. React to that.

00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:48.797
I feel trapped right now.

00:09:50.173 --> 00:09:53.093
-Are you content with how they're...
-They're nervous. It is what it is.

00:09:53.176 --> 00:09:55.303
It's not a YouTube, so I'm not gonna...

00:09:55.387 --> 00:09:57.722
We're already at the point where
we're forcing it,

00:09:57.806 --> 00:09:59.182
-so let's just let them be them.
-Perfect.

00:09:59.265 --> 00:10:00.642
Start the money counter!

00:10:00.725 --> 00:10:02.102
Let's see what your price is.

00:10:02.185 --> 00:10:03.853
I know Brett's gonna do a deal.

00:10:03.937 --> 00:10:05.563
We're up to $40,000.

00:10:05.939 --> 00:10:07.273
That's really nice. Steady.

00:10:07.357 --> 00:10:10.360
We're at $100,000 already.

00:10:10.443 --> 00:10:14.656
Jimmy is so good at making a bribe
feel as visual as possible.

00:10:14.739 --> 00:10:16.241
It's not just the counter going up,

00:10:16.324 --> 00:10:19.202
it's also the cash piling up every second.

00:10:19.285 --> 00:10:21.079
If you press the button right now,

00:10:21.162 --> 00:10:22.872
you would get that pile of money.

00:10:24.958 --> 00:10:26.334
$600,000.

00:10:26.418 --> 00:10:27.377
How do you feel, Cory?

00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:29.671
You're the one who has the least
amount of money out of us.

00:10:29.754 --> 00:10:31.631
I mean, 720 grand...

00:10:31.715 --> 00:10:33.258
That's a lot of money.

00:10:33.341 --> 00:10:34.843
-Think it's gonna stop at a million?
-970!

00:10:34.926 --> 00:10:37.012
-It could stop at a million.
-990!

00:10:37.095 --> 00:10:37.929
Nobody's taking it.

00:10:38.013 --> 00:10:40.515
One million dollars!

00:10:40.598 --> 00:10:42.392
-Somebody pressed it.
-Yeah, Brett pressed it.

00:10:42.475 --> 00:10:44.561
Congratulations, you're now a millionaire.

00:10:44.936 --> 00:10:46.980
Brett, go to your money right now.

00:10:47.063 --> 00:10:48.523
Come to your million dollars.

00:10:48.606 --> 00:10:49.691
Come on in!

00:10:51.693 --> 00:10:52.861
Brett played a good game.

00:10:52.944 --> 00:10:55.739
-Brett, let's go smash your heart.
-Okay.

00:10:55.822 --> 00:10:57.115
You wanna drop him with the bag?

00:10:57.198 --> 00:10:59.034
Yeah, that, and then the guards
just start throwing them.

00:10:59.117 --> 00:11:00.869
We're packing it as quickly as possible.

00:11:01.244 --> 00:11:03.580
Seeing you jump in the money,
that must've been a surreal moment.

00:11:03.663 --> 00:11:06.750
It was really cool.
I was really nervous about being here.

00:11:06.833 --> 00:11:09.294
I don't wanna be on TV.
I had all these doubts.

00:11:09.377 --> 00:11:12.380
And then I talked to my fiancée, she said,
"Be gone as long as you need to be."

00:11:12.464 --> 00:11:13.757
"Just make it worth it."

00:11:13.840 --> 00:11:15.383
And she supported me 100%.

00:11:15.467 --> 00:11:16.801
So I got on the plane.

00:11:16.885 --> 00:11:18.845
And then here we are, six weeks later,

00:11:18.928 --> 00:11:20.555
and $1.2 million later.

00:11:20.638 --> 00:11:22.015
It's so freaking cool.

00:11:24.392 --> 00:11:25.518
-Let's do it.
-Let's do it.

00:11:25.602 --> 00:11:26.936
Last game.

00:11:30.023 --> 00:11:33.860
Just trying to make sure that this episode
finishes on time.

00:11:33.943 --> 00:11:35.195
Here we go.

00:11:35.278 --> 00:11:37.530
We gotta get the briefcases,
we gotta get the check.

00:11:40.658 --> 00:11:42.869
Are you watching the finale
from last season?

00:11:42.952 --> 00:11:44.662
Yeah, just seeing how we edited it.

00:11:44.746 --> 00:11:46.164
&lt;i&gt;Bring in the blindfolds!&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:46.247 --> 00:11:49.000
Do you have any thoughts as you look back
on last year's finale?

00:11:50.210 --> 00:11:51.670
I wonder what time we were filming.

00:11:52.128 --> 00:11:53.296
That was like at 6:00 a.m.

00:11:56.716 --> 00:11:58.134
I'm tired as hell.

00:12:02.305 --> 00:12:05.725
How do you feel?
Final game, final episode.

00:12:05.809 --> 00:12:08.269
We got two really good finalists.

00:12:08.353 --> 00:12:11.398
I think we got great story,
two family men.

00:12:11.481 --> 00:12:13.692
It's been a wild ride.

00:12:13.775 --> 00:12:16.277
From the storm in Las Vegas,

00:12:16.361 --> 00:12:17.987
to the City,

00:12:18.071 --> 00:12:20.573
to the white room with the four games,

00:12:20.657 --> 00:12:25.120
and the guy who tried to grab it
and missed it by inches,

00:12:25.203 --> 00:12:28.206
to the thunderstorm
where we had to push a day,

00:12:28.289 --> 00:12:31.001
and then we finally got our day
in the obstacle course

00:12:31.084 --> 00:12:33.586
to going out to Fiji with Jeff Probst,

00:12:33.670 --> 00:12:36.423
to coming back
and reintroducing the cubes,

00:12:36.506 --> 00:12:39.092
to then doing the Strong Game
100 feet in the air,

00:12:39.175 --> 00:12:40.927
something we've wanted to do forever,

00:12:41.011 --> 00:12:43.263
then we have this massive Smart Game,

00:12:43.346 --> 00:12:45.724
to burying 10 people at once

00:12:45.807 --> 00:12:47.767
and doing a $1,000,000 bribe with them,

00:12:47.851 --> 00:12:49.144
down to right here.

00:12:49.769 --> 00:12:52.022
It's been a crazy 40-plus days

00:12:52.439 --> 00:12:54.858
and Jon literally questioning everybody.

00:12:55.900 --> 00:12:57.027
It's 4:00 a.m.

00:12:57.110 --> 00:13:02.323
I really appreciate everyone continually
showing up with a smile on your face.

00:13:02.407 --> 00:13:04.325
This is the schedule from tonight.

00:13:04.409 --> 00:13:08.038
We're an hour behind
when the show was supposed to wrap.

00:13:08.121 --> 00:13:09.247
I showed this to Jimmy,

00:13:09.330 --> 00:13:10.498
and you know what he did
to this piece of paper?

00:13:10.582 --> 00:13:12.500
Well, something like this?

00:13:12.584 --> 00:13:14.627
-Yeah.
-That's pretty much what it is.

00:13:14.711 --> 00:13:17.047
When we play the final game,
everyone will be gone?

00:13:17.130 --> 00:13:19.716
Yeah. We're clearing everyone,
they got blindfolds.

00:13:19.799 --> 00:13:22.302
And there's no one watching
the control room or anything?

00:13:22.385 --> 00:13:24.012
I had them shut everything off.

00:13:24.095 --> 00:13:26.014
We're right outside the control center,

00:13:26.097 --> 00:13:28.266
and Jimmy was adamant
about cutting the feed

00:13:28.350 --> 00:13:31.770
so not even the extended crew
knows who won.

00:13:31.853 --> 00:13:33.355
All right, here we go.

00:13:33.438 --> 00:13:36.816
One of you is not gonna have $5,000,000.

00:13:36.900 --> 00:13:39.235
I promise you,
the other person understands,

00:13:39.319 --> 00:13:41.529
if you win $5,000,000,
you go insane.

00:13:41.613 --> 00:13:42.739
Lose your freaking mind.

00:13:42.822 --> 00:13:44.491
Get them both to yell right before.

00:13:45.325 --> 00:13:46.284
Right before, yeah.

00:13:46.368 --> 00:13:50.288
To get the energy up, real quick,
I think we should all give a loud yell.

00:13:50.372 --> 00:13:52.832
Three, two, one...

00:13:54.209 --> 00:13:55.085
Let's go!

00:13:55.168 --> 00:13:57.087
-That's good.
-There we go.

00:13:57.170 --> 00:13:58.630
That was what we needed.

00:13:58.713 --> 00:13:59.881
Yeah. That was great.

00:13:59.964 --> 00:14:02.884
One of you is gonna be handed
this $5,000,000 check.

00:14:02.967 --> 00:14:05.303
You can put it
in whatever briefcase you want,

00:14:05.387 --> 00:14:07.055
and if either of you guesses correctly,

00:14:07.138 --> 00:14:09.099
you are a multi-millionaire.

00:14:09.182 --> 00:14:11.434
I need all our camera people
to turn around.

00:14:11.518 --> 00:14:14.437
This is a battle between Cory and Tyler

00:14:14.521 --> 00:14:16.523
and no one else on the planet.

00:14:20.527 --> 00:14:21.569
All right, Jimmy.

00:14:21.653 --> 00:14:23.279
-Am I good to turn around?
-You are.

00:14:23.363 --> 00:14:26.658
Okay. Camera crew,
you can point the cameras over here.

00:14:26.741 --> 00:14:28.785
Cory, turn around
and take the blindfold off.

00:14:30.036 --> 00:14:31.371
What can you tell me about 9?

00:14:31.454 --> 00:14:32.706
Is the check inside here?

00:14:32.997 --> 00:14:34.374
Open it and find out.

00:14:35.458 --> 00:14:36.543
I'm gonna go with 9.

00:14:38.503 --> 00:14:39.462
Throw it off the stage.

00:14:40.338 --> 00:14:42.215
We will be taking this briefcase
out of play.

00:14:44.175 --> 00:14:45.510
Just cost me ten grand.

00:14:45.593 --> 00:14:49.639
Cory is in possession
of the $5,000,000 check.

00:14:50.098 --> 00:14:51.683
Now there's one less case.

00:14:52.934 --> 00:14:54.019
Tyler, turn around.

00:14:54.102 --> 00:14:55.353
Take off your blindfold.

00:14:56.730 --> 00:14:59.065
-What about 2?
-Open it and find out.

00:14:59.482 --> 00:15:01.901
He's deploying Tyler's strategy
back at him.

00:15:02.360 --> 00:15:03.570
He's officially chosen 5!

00:15:04.279 --> 00:15:05.196
There's no check.

00:15:07.866 --> 00:15:10.326
So it has to be 6...

00:15:11.119 --> 00:15:12.287
or 8.

00:15:14.330 --> 00:15:15.540
I'm gonna go with 6.

00:15:16.750 --> 00:15:17.917
Was it in this one?

00:15:18.001 --> 00:15:19.878
-That'd be crazy, if so.
-Yeah, it is.

00:15:19.961 --> 00:15:21.421
Really?

00:15:21.504 --> 00:15:23.131
No shot. Are you joking?

00:15:23.214 --> 00:15:24.632
It was in 8.

00:15:24.716 --> 00:15:26.176
I was so close.

00:15:26.259 --> 00:15:27.761
That just doesn't even feel real.

00:15:29.763 --> 00:15:33.767
It's so crazy to only see
four briefcases on this table.

00:15:33.850 --> 00:15:35.935
Is there $5,000,000 in that briefcase?

00:15:36.644 --> 00:15:39.189
It's red! Oh, no!

00:15:39.481 --> 00:15:42.442
Have you ever been on a shoot
this long in your life?

00:15:43.777 --> 00:15:44.986
Believe it or not...

00:15:45.779 --> 00:15:46.821
yes.

00:15:51.409 --> 00:15:53.244
You're going with 3?
Wait, before you open it...

00:15:53.328 --> 00:15:55.163
Get ready. Get ready, bro.

00:15:55.246 --> 00:15:57.248
Did you hit it? Are you a millionaire?

00:15:57.749 --> 00:15:58.667
Go to light.

00:16:01.503 --> 00:16:03.004
Let's go!

00:16:05.882 --> 00:16:08.051
Let's go!

00:16:08.134 --> 00:16:09.386
Come on!

00:16:09.469 --> 00:16:11.429
-You did it!
-Let's go!

00:16:11.513 --> 00:16:12.555
You did it!

00:16:12.639 --> 00:16:15.016
He hit it!

00:16:15.100 --> 00:16:16.142
Oh, my God.

00:16:16.226 --> 00:16:17.644
Get on the money!

00:16:21.648 --> 00:16:22.816
All right, don't fall.

00:16:22.899 --> 00:16:25.610
$5,000,000 Tyler just won,
and look at Cory.

00:16:27.237 --> 00:16:31.074
Bro, you're literally standing
on your mountain of money.

00:16:31.157 --> 00:16:33.993
Tyler, you just won Season 2
of &lt;i&gt;Beast Games.&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:34.077 --> 00:16:36.913
Tyler just won Season 2 of &lt;i&gt;Beast Games&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:36.996 --> 00:16:39.332
and $5,000,000!

00:16:39.416 --> 00:16:40.375
Bro.

00:16:40.458 --> 00:16:43.753
I can't wait to see
your wife and kids' reactions.

00:16:45.046 --> 00:16:47.549
Man, I feel bad for Cory.

00:17:25.754 --> 00:17:27.756
-I love you guys so much.
-I love you, Dad.

00:17:33.428 --> 00:17:34.721
I'm really happy for Tyler.

00:17:34.804 --> 00:17:38.391
If somebody could've won other than me,
I'm happy that it was him.

00:17:38.475 --> 00:17:42.312
I'm gonna love the Lord
in the good times and the bad times.

00:17:43.355 --> 00:17:46.232
Cory has officially been eliminated.

00:17:46.983 --> 00:17:47.942
And this hurts.

00:17:55.033 --> 00:17:56.368
All right, Russ, go for it.

00:17:56.451 --> 00:18:00.288
Three, two, one, go!

00:18:00.372 --> 00:18:04.709
We officially have a winner
of Season 2 of &lt;i&gt;Beast Games!&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:04.793 --> 00:18:06.461
Congratulations!

00:18:07.671 --> 00:18:09.923
Congrats on winning Season 2!

00:18:10.882 --> 00:18:12.884
Thank you so much for watching
all the way till the end.

00:18:12.967 --> 00:18:15.428
I can't wait to see what you think
of Season 3.

00:18:15.512 --> 00:18:16.638
I lost my voice.

00:18:17.681 --> 00:18:19.516
-One more.
-Okay.

00:18:19.599 --> 00:18:21.518
Tyler, just keep throwing up money
if you can.

00:18:21.601 --> 00:18:23.687
And I can't wait to blow your mind
with Season 3.

00:18:23.770 --> 00:18:25.647
Trust me, it's gonna be way better.

00:18:26.690 --> 00:18:28.525
Look at the lighting and everything.

00:18:28.608 --> 00:18:29.776
Oh, my God.

00:18:29.859 --> 00:18:31.444
I feel on top of the world, man.

00:18:31.528 --> 00:18:33.238
I lost my voice from yelling.

00:18:33.321 --> 00:18:36.116
When I was serving a year in Korea
by myself,

00:18:36.199 --> 00:18:38.410
I've missed out on half of my kids' lives.

00:18:38.493 --> 00:18:42.372
Winning this just gives me a chance
to just be dad

00:18:42.455 --> 00:18:44.499
and they don't have to worry
about when dad's coming back,

00:18:44.582 --> 00:18:48.003
because my oldest is four
and he has a hard time when I leave.

00:18:48.586 --> 00:18:51.047
And when my wife came to visit us
in the City,

00:18:51.131 --> 00:18:52.966
she was telling me that
he was having a hard time

00:18:53.049 --> 00:18:54.884
struggling without me there.

00:18:56.302 --> 00:18:58.513
I don't want him to have to
experience that.

00:18:58.596 --> 00:19:02.017
So I think I'll get out of the military,
we'll be able to retire,

00:19:02.100 --> 00:19:04.394
and just spend time with our kids
and do what we want.

00:19:04.477 --> 00:19:06.104
It's a dream come true.

00:19:06.187 --> 00:19:08.273
I missed you guys so much.

00:19:08.356 --> 00:19:09.274
Dada.

00:19:09.983 --> 00:19:12.444
Jimmy, how are you gonna top this
for Season 3?

00:19:12.527 --> 00:19:14.404
Don't you worry. I mean, you saw...

00:19:17.115 --> 00:19:18.491
How do I have that much hair on my neck?

00:19:22.328 --> 00:19:23.580
Congratulations!

00:19:25.290 --> 00:19:27.292
They're all celebrating
that we just wrapped filming.

00:19:27.375 --> 00:19:29.169
Do you get emotional at moments like this?

00:19:29.252 --> 00:19:30.670
You just changed that guy's life.

00:19:30.754 --> 00:19:34.382
I would be more emotional if I didn't
just film for 15 hours straight.

00:19:34.799 --> 00:19:36.634
I'm struggling to keep my eyes open.

00:19:36.718 --> 00:19:39.095
I'm worried in the cut
I'm gonna look sleepy.

00:19:39.846 --> 00:19:43.266
Do you take a moment
to enjoy these milestones...

00:19:43.350 --> 00:19:46.061
No, I'm about to fly to Africa tomorrow
to film a main channel video.

00:19:46.144 --> 00:19:48.897
I don't even get half a day off
to celebrate.

00:19:49.898 --> 00:19:51.149
We finished.

00:19:51.232 --> 00:19:52.525
Tyler, we survived.

00:19:52.609 --> 00:19:54.444
-Me Tyler?
-You Tyler.

00:19:54.527 --> 00:19:56.863
No more casting other Tylers.
It's so confusing.

00:19:56.946 --> 00:19:59.532
Can you take a moment
and enjoy this, Tyler, or...

00:19:59.616 --> 00:20:01.201
No, I will enjoy this.

00:20:01.284 --> 00:20:03.036
This is too big of a project
not to enjoy it.

00:20:03.119 --> 00:20:04.579
He's gonna enjoy it by sleeping
for four days straight.

00:20:04.662 --> 00:20:06.664
I'm gonna sleep for four days straight.
I'm very excited.

00:20:06.748 --> 00:20:09.334
He's gonna sleep for four days,
enjoy it for a day,

00:20:09.417 --> 00:20:10.960
and then start writing Season 3.

00:20:11.044 --> 00:20:12.879
That and post as well.

00:20:12.962 --> 00:20:15.423
Yeah, and how does this shot look?
Does it look insane?

00:20:15.507 --> 00:20:19.177
Just sitting on $5,000,000
with this big frigging set.

00:20:21.888 --> 00:20:22.806
Let me ask you...

00:20:22.889 --> 00:20:25.392
This whole 10-episode series,
you've been asking me questions,

00:20:25.475 --> 00:20:27.227
-let me ask you some.
-Hit me, Jimmy.

00:20:27.310 --> 00:20:30.146
Do you think this will perform better
or worse than Season 1?

00:20:30.230 --> 00:20:31.773
This? Yeah, of course.

00:20:31.856 --> 00:20:34.526
I feel like everything was bigger
and more thought out.

00:20:34.609 --> 00:20:37.570
And I personally got to know
the contestants even more.

00:20:37.654 --> 00:20:40.824
I feel that's something that the viewers
will feel as well.

00:20:40.907 --> 00:20:42.534
Yeah. I do too.

00:20:42.617 --> 00:20:44.202
You guys poured a lot into this.

00:20:44.285 --> 00:20:46.913
Yeah, you saw some days,
we had over 1,000 people working on it.

00:20:46.996 --> 00:20:48.498
These are monster projects.

00:20:48.581 --> 00:20:50.667
It's kind of funny
because I watch old interviews

00:20:50.750 --> 00:20:53.670
I'd say stuff like, "In an optimal world,
if my eyes are open, I'm filming."

00:20:54.587 --> 00:20:55.547
"Like, why would I not?"

00:20:55.630 --> 00:20:57.716
And I see them, and I'm like, "Frig."

00:20:57.799 --> 00:20:59.884
That's why I'm in this scenario right now.

00:21:01.052 --> 00:21:02.429
Jimmy, I just want to say thank you.

00:21:02.512 --> 00:21:05.140
Yeah, thank you.
Are you doing an outro to this?

00:21:05.223 --> 00:21:07.267
I'll let you take it, man.

00:21:07.350 --> 00:21:09.477
I'm so grateful for having us,
our entire crew,

00:21:09.561 --> 00:21:11.354
you guys being so inclusive...

00:21:11.438 --> 00:21:13.481
-Letting me document and capture.
-We didn't hide anything.

00:21:13.565 --> 00:21:15.025
It'll be interesting to see
how it turns out.

00:21:15.108 --> 00:21:16.860
But also subscribe to him.
He doesn't have a million subscribers.

00:21:16.943 --> 00:21:18.278
It's kind of pissing me off.

00:21:18.361 --> 00:21:20.530
He does like 3,000,000 views a video.
It doesn't make sense.

00:21:21.698 --> 00:21:22.824
Thanks, Jimmy.

00:21:22.907 --> 00:21:24.659
-Appreciate you having me, man.
-Yeah, thank you.

00:21:24.743 --> 00:21:26.870
You've crushed it. Go back to your baby.

00:21:27.996 --> 00:21:29.622
You're allowed to see your baby again.

00:21:29.706 --> 00:21:30.957
-I love you, man.
-Bro.

00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:34.377
I just want to say thank you all
before I head out.

00:21:34.461 --> 00:21:37.005
Appreciate you guys. Turned out amazing.
Thank you.

